<article class="env-lemma" id="00GE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00GE">Lemma <span data-tag="00GE">10.35.22</span>.</a> With notation as above. Assume that $R$ is a Noetherian Jacobson ring. Further assume $R \to S$ is of finite type. There is a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \text{Constr}(Y) \ar[r]^{E \mapsto E_0} \ar[d]^{E \mapsto f(E)} &  \text{Constr}(Y_0) \ar[d]^{E \mapsto f(E)} \\  \text{Constr}(X) \ar[r]^{E \mapsto E_0} &  \text{Constr}(X_0) }  \]
</div>
  <p> where the horizontal arrows are the bijections from Topology, Lemma <a href="/tag/005Y" data-tag="005Y">5.18.8</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $R \to S$ is of finite type, it is of finite presentation, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00FP" data-tag="00FP">10.31.4</a>. Thus the image of a constructible set in $X$ is constructible in $Y$ by Chevalley's theorem (Theorem <a href="/tag/00FE" data-tag="00FE">10.29.10</a>). Combined with Lemma <a href="/tag/00GD" data-tag="00GD">10.35.21</a> the lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>